00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:56,220
 But then, when we're talking about Lambda, there were some trade-offs, let's call them, or choices that were made for the Lambda event handler model.

41
00:06:56,220 --> 00:07:01,220
 There was only ever one request per environment. It was a great thing when it was built.

42
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:06,220
 Because it meant you didn't need to think about strange, multi-concurrent things going on in one environment.

43
00:07:06,220 --> 00:07:12,220
 It was super secure, one execution would never trample on another execution. That was great.

44
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:20,220
 We had to pick 15 minutes. Lambda started with one minute, and it's grown up to 15 minutes for a Lambda event function.

45
00:07:20,220 --> 00:07:24,220
 But that was a choice to make, to be able to manage the service.

46
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:30,220
 Billing on the war clock time, so a Lambda function used to start, used to finish, and you would pay for the whole time.

47
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:35,220
 And then, the sandbox that Lambda runs in, I'm coming back to that firecracker sandbox again.

48
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:39,220
 You never ever saw that, or had any, could ever control that.

49
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:41,220
 But that was part of Lambda.

50
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:45,220
 And so these were choices for the Lambda you used to love and know.

51
00:07:45,220 --> 00:07:49,220
 But customers and people have been asking to do a little bit more.

